-- title:
--   Bounded functional calculus P(f) and the time evolution U(t) = exp(−itA)
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be a projection-valued measure on $\mathfrak H$ with spectral measures $\mu_\psi$. For a bounded Borel function $f : \mathbb R \to \mathbb C$, $P(f) = \int_{\mathbb R} f(\lambda)\, dP(\lambda)$ is the bounded operator on $\mathfrak H$ characterized by
--   $$\langle \psi, P(f)\psi\rangle = \int_{\mathbb R} f(\lambda)\, d\mu_\psi(\lambda) \qquad (\psi \in \mathfrak H).$$
--   If $A = \int \lambda\, dP(\lambda)$, then $f(A) = P(f)$. The **time evolution** generated by $A$ is
--   $$U(t) = \mathrm e^{-\mathrm i t A} = P\big(\lambda \mapsto \mathrm e^{-\mathrm i t\lambda}\big), \qquad t \in \mathbb R,$$
--   so that $\psi(t) = \mathrm e^{-\mathrm itA}\psi$ solves the Schrödinger equation $\mathrm i \frac{d}{dt}\psi(t) = A\psi(t)$, and $\mathrm e^{\mathrm itA} = U(-t)$.
--
--   This one definition is shared by every chunk of the series that uses it and is reviewed once for all of them. It serves:
--
--   - chunk `05-rage`: pp. 123–124, Theorem 5.1; p. 128, Theorem 5.6, Eq. (5.13); p. 129, Theorem 5.7, Eq. (5.14); p. 130, Theorem 5.8, Eq. (5.18); p. 130, Corollary 5.9, Eqs. (5.19)–(5.20)
--   - chunk `14-scattering`: p. 247, Section 12.1, Eq. (12.3); p. 248, Lemma 12.1; p. 248, Theorem 12.2, Eq. (12.8); p. 249, Lemma 12.3, Eqs. (12.11)–(12.12); p. 249, Theorem 12.4
--
--   **Formalization Note.** `boundedSpectralIntegral P f` is the operator $T$ with $\langle\psi, T\psi\rangle = \int f\, d\mu_\psi$ for all $\psi$ (unique over $\mathbb C$), chosen by `Classical.choose`, and the zero operator if none exists; that never happens for a projection-valued measure and a bounded Borel $f$. `timeEvolution P t` applies it to $\lambda \mapsto \mathrm e^{-\mathrm it\lambda}$.
-- source:
--   Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, AMS GSM 99, 2009, p. 90, Section 3.1, Eqs. (3.17), (3.20), and p. 123, Section 5.1

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_TeschlQM_Shared_spectralMeasure

open MeasureTheory
open scoped ENNReal InnerProductSpace

namespace TeschlQM.Shared

open Classical in
/-- Teschl, p. 90, (3.17), (3.20): for a bounded Borel function `f`, `P(f) = ∫_ℝ f(λ) dP(λ)` as a
bounded operator on `ℌ`: the bounded operator `T` with `⟨ψ, Tψ⟩ = ∫_ℝ f(λ) dμ_ψ(λ)` for all
`ψ ∈ ℌ` (over `ℂ` a bounded operator is determined by its quadratic form, so there is at most
one); the zero operator if there is none, which never happens for a projection-valued measure
and a bounded Borel `f`. -/
noncomputable def boundedSpectralIntegral {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]
    [CompleteSpace H] (P : Set ℝ → (H →L[ℂ] H)) (f : ℝ → ℂ) : H →L[ℂ] H :=
  if h : ∃ T : H →L[ℂ] H, ∀ ψ : H, ⟪ψ, T ψ⟫_ℂ = ∫ x, f x ∂spectralMeasure P ψ then h.choose
  else 0

/-- Teschl, p. 123, Sec. 5.1: the **time evolution** `U(t) = exp(−itA)` of the self-adjoint
operator `A = ∫ λ dP(λ)`, defined by the functional calculus as `P(f_t)` with the bounded
continuous function `f_t(λ) = e^{−itλ}`. In particular `e^{itA} = timeEvolution P (−t)`. -/
noncomputable def timeEvolution {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]
    [CompleteSpace H] (P : Set ℝ → (H →L[ℂ] H)) (t : ℝ) : H →L[ℂ] H :=
  boundedSpectralIntegral P (fun x : ℝ => Complex.exp (-(Complex.I * (t : ℂ) * (x : ℂ))))

end TeschlQM.Shared


